{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a74154184a970cb13","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are the independent SEED AUTHOR for round 3 of an adversarial review (\"gauntlet\") of a game-engine skill framework. The framework (capability map, skill hierarchy, contracts, configurations, radar, legacy catalogue, milestones) lives in /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework (data/*.json is the source of truth; scripts/check.py is a structural validator; docs/ are rendered/handwritten views). Fifteen blind critics will review a COPY of it. Your job is to plant realistic defects (\"seeds\") in that copy so we can measure critic recall. You work independently of the builder; never write into the repository itself.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create the copy: `mkdir -p /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r3 && cp -r /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r3/` then in the copy delete the `gauntlet/round-1`, `gauntlet/round-2` directories and `docs/06-gap-analysis.md`'s nothing (keep docs), and remove any `__pycache__`. Keep gauntlet/PROTOCOL.md. Also create an empty `gauntlet/round-3/` directory in the copy.\n2. Read enough of the copy's data to plant 15 seeds, exactly one per critic mandate below. Each seed must be: realistic (the kind of error a careful builder could make), material (a critic in that mandate should flag it as major/blocker), INVISIBLE to `python3 scripts/check.py` (run it in the copy after planting: it must report 0 errors — check.py now verifies many things: capability ids referenced inside capability names exist, radar class equals maturity and radar owner lineage, X/S capabilities carry only the 'experimental' profile, per-platform implementers, milestone closure and contract freeze order, legacy stance capabilities, untrusted-input registry, authoring paths, oracle authors… so pick defect kinds it cannot see: wrong owner among plausible skills, deleted capability not referenced by id anywhere, subtle legacy wording in a name, wrong-but-plausible contract summary, missing consumer edge where the edge is optional anyway, dishonest maturity that you keep consistent with the radar, overlapping capability under a different wording, wrong target/platform tag that still closes, etc.). If you delete a capability, also remove every reference to its id (seed-map terms may be remapped to a neighbouring capability, radar/legacy/milestone gates edited) so check.py stays green. Vary the defect kinds; do not reuse round-2's seeds: motion vectors owned by post, deleted safe reclamation, deleted CCD, deleted lag compensation, deleted undo/transactions, console tagged pc, deleted cross-pool arbitration, deleted ICU message formatting, deleted key custody, deleted golden-image tests, duplicated GPU instance data, game-thread/render-thread wording, work graphs labelled established, deleted delta patching, deleted retargeting.\n   Mandates (one seed each): K-ARCH (boundaries/overlaps/contracts), K-RENDER (rendering), K-SYSTEMS (concurrency/memory/IO/frame), K-SIM (physics/simulation), K-NET (networking), K-TOOLS (editor/content pipeline), K-PLATFORM (platforms/PAL/consoles/mobile/web), K-PERF (performance architecture & organization), K-PROD (production/release/lifecycle), K-FUTURE (maturity honesty/future tech), K-COMPLETE (a genuinely missing capability — delete one clearly needed, established capability), K-LEGACY (legacy architecture stated as a default), K-GAMEPLAY (animation/audio/AI/UI/localization/accessibility/gameplay), K-TEST (testing/validation), K-SEC (security/privacy).\n3. Re-render docs in the copy: `cd <copy> && python3 scripts/render.py` so generated docs reflect the seeds (docs/01-05, 09). Confirm `python3 scripts/check.py` = 0 errors and `python3 scripts/render.py --check` = current.\n4. Write the sealed seed list to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r3-seeds.json as a JSON list of [seed_id \"S01\".., critic_id, one-line description of the planted defect, the exact data edit you made].\nYour final message must NOT describe the seeds (the builder must stay blind until after the round). Final message: one line: \"planted N seeds; check.py green; copy at <path>; seeds sealed at <path>\"."},"uuid":"d5ecc659-12e0-4934-83f1-9a336125295e","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:55:06.688Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
